{
 "duration": 54.382,
 "sentences": [
  {
   "index": 0,
   "start": 0.25,
   "end": 5.938,
   "text": "TypeScript seven just broke Angular's compiler. So Angular is rewriting part of it, in Rust."
  },
  {
   "index": 1,
   "start": 6.338,
   "end": 13.709,
   "text": "Here's why. TypeScript seven is the native rewrite, in Go. Much faster. But it shipped without the transformer API."
  },
  {
   "index": 2,
   "start": 14.089,
   "end": 21.852,
   "text": "And Angular's compiler, ngc, plugged straight into that API, to turn your decorators and templates into JavaScript."
  },
  {
   "index": 3,
   "start": 22.232,
   "end": 33.33,
   "text": "So the team built ngp, the Angular preprocessor. A Rust front end, built on Oxc, scans your files in parallel, finds every component, and resolves its metadata."
  },
  {
   "index": 4,
   "start": 33.71,
   "end": 39.146,
   "text": "Then it hands off. Type checking and bundling go to tools like tsgo, esbuild, or Rolldown."
  },
  {
   "index": 5,
   "start": 39.526,
   "end": 43.175,
   "text": "Early community benchmarks show builds up to three times faster."
  },
  {
   "index": 6,
   "start": 43.555,
   "end": 47.382,
   "text": "But it's still in beta. For production, stay on ngc for now."
  },
  {
   "index": 7,
   "start": 47.802,
   "end": 53.482,
   "text": "The lesson? Your framework is only as fast as the tools underneath it. And those tools are going native."
  }
 ],
